        "created_at": "2015-09-04T01:27:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I played a 4-player game of Deck Building tonight with some new players and some questions came up.</p><p>Suppose you have 4 screws in your hand. You buy a card that costs 4 screws. Clearly you cannot buy another card. But can you still build a card from your hand? The rule book does not say otherwise, so we've been playing that you can.</p><p>A question came up about what stairs were worth for purchasing other cards. Re-checking the rule book now, I see that it does mention that stairs are not worth any screws.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:45:21.664Z",
